:       \"Math and Number Theory\",\r\n27:       \"Recursion\"\r\n28:     ],\r\n29:     \"summary\": \"Find indices of two numbers that add up to a target using a dictionary for instant lookups.\",\r\n30:     \"examples\": [\r\n31:       {\r\n32:         \"input\": \"nums = [2, 7, 11, 15]\",\r\n33:         \"output\": \"Computed via twoSum(nums, 9)\",\r\n34:         \"explanation\": \"Step through the execution in the visualizer to inspect how variables mutate to produce the result.\"\r\n35:       }\r\n36:     ],\r\n37:     \"constraints\": [\r\n38:       \"1 <= nums.length <= 10^4\",\r\n39:       \"-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4\",\r\n40:       \"Memory limit: 256 MB, Time limit: 2.0 seconds\"\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
